"Hm? And what business have you lot here?
I've no interest in the people of the land, you know.{w}Or will you perhaps entertain me somehow?"{w}{p}"Well, no matter. I was bored myself;
this should do nicely to pass the time.{w}Now then, what manner of creature are you? Name yourselves."{w}{p}"...Honestly, this is what comes of lowborn rabble.
Perhaps naming myself first would be amusing in its own way?{w}I am Asunamuchi, the Heavenly Fiend. Mark it well."{w}

"Here in Miasuna there are heaps upon heaps of books
chronicling the history of this land in fine detail."{w}{p}"I have whiled away the time with them,
but of late even that has... grown a touch tiresome."{w}{p}"Come now, you lot.{w}Do something to entertain me.{w}I am bored, you hear?"{w}

"Ho? You lot have grown
rather formidable, haven't you?"{w}{p}"Since that day, nothing amusing has happened, you see.
I am bored.{w}Come, play with me and stave off my boredom."{w}

{0E}"You may have beaten me, but it's already too late...
Heh heh heh heh...{0F}
Urgh!"{w}

"...You have some skill."{w}{p}"However,
we mages, who stand at the apex of the hierarchy of knowledge,
have no cause to give way to fools."{w}{p}"Remember that... and remember it well."{w}

You stopped in your tracks.{w}No -- you could not go one step further.{w}{p}The monster that had been about to cross your path
noticed its prey and clattered its jawbone.{w}It was a symbol of death, notorious even among adventurers.{w}{p}Why had it appeared here?{w}Why, gripped by such terror, could you not move?{w}Why did it have to be you who ran into it?{w}{p}All manner of thoughts must have flashed through your minds.{w}But there is no need to worry.{w}{p}However much you rage at the injustice of it,{w}however much you tremble in fear,{w}it will all be over in a matter of moments.{w}{p}Had it been waiting for you to steel yourselves?{w}Bones rattling in the silence, the dreadful monster
slowly raised its scythe...{w}

{0E}"I just have to kill them, right?
Kill these guys and you'll be satisfied, right...{0F}
Numbra Narv!!"{w}

{0E}You held up the Light Rank you had obtained
in the Sanctum of Genesis.{0F}
Rafa's body was enveloped in a warm light.{w}{p}The Sun Spirit who guards the True Crystal
began to shine brighter than ever before.{w}

"Ah, what wonderful power...{w}Now I won't have to burn up my own life...{w}I can keep on shining forever...!"{w}{p}"It wasn't the suffering itself I hated."{w}{p}"What hurt was not being able to keep shining
on all the people of this land I love so dearly."{w}{p}"...But thanks to all of you,
it looks like I can shine on them forever now."{w}

Hand in hand, Rafa and Yorfa would surely
go on protecting this land.{w}{p}Along with the warm light, a deep, gentle sense
of fulfillment wrapped around you.{w}

"The Palace of the Sun draws ever closer
to our world, the Dark Realm.
All according to Master Mayer's will..."{w}

"Such things are of no consequence."{w}{p}"Serving not a god but Master Mayer,
and touching the deaths of mortals...
that, for me, is the greatest of joys..."{w}

"Yes. If things go on like this,
all the Sun Spirit can do is waste away.{w}You must carry out the rescue with your own power."{w}{p}"And what must you do to that end?
You know, don't you?"{w}

"Enough of this farce.
You, stay out of the way now."{w}{p}"In any case, that Sun Spirit is past saving.{w}Your stubborn insistence that all is well
is touching, I'll grant you."{w}

"Ah, Rafa..."{w}{p}"You're suffering,
and I can't save you..."{w}{p}"I, too... with you, as we were long ago...{w}The two of us, like back when we
watched over the land in Nertowa..."{w}

"......{w}O king of our Dark Realm..."{w}{p}"I could not live up to your expectations...
Forgive... me..."{w}{p}"Numbra Male...m...
may this world... be... yours...{w}Uuugh... Gwaaah...!!"{w}

{0E}                                              
                 In the Light                 
                                              {0F}{w}

"Welcome to the fairy village, after your long journey.
I am Meem, the Fairy King."{w}{p}"This is the hidden village of the fairies.
What business have you here, people of the land?"{w}{p}"Whether you came by design or by chance, I know not.{w}But mind your conduct.{w}The folk of this village do not think kindly of the people of the land."{w}

"The land you live on is maintained by our brethren.
Were you aware of that fact?"{w}{p}"Though we live hidden away in the fairy village,
even we cannot be indifferent to the affairs of the land.{w}We, too, love the land."{w}{p}"I do not mean to lay a debt upon you.{w}It is only that you must never forget it.{w}I would have you engrave it upon your hearts."{w}

"To maintain the land itself...{w}I, Meem, the Fairy King, have never forgotten
their devotion, not for a single moment."{w}{p}"The land is the world itself.{w}Without the world, no one can live."{w}{p}"That is no less true for us.
Whatever the past may have been, that fact does not change."{w}

{0E}                                            
                  Updraft                   
                                            {0F}{w}

"Shall I lend you a hand?"{w}{p}"Thanks to Ruu and Makakuri helping me out,
I got to see my dear wicked mage,
and my business in this land is mostly finished."{w}{p}"So maybe I can be of some use to you."{w}

"I'm sorry this is the only way we can ask.{w}Will you do this for us?"{w}{p}"We have allowed many Demon Dukes to invade.{w}We want you to defeat every one of them
and bring back proof."{w}{p}"I'm counting on you. With the power that drove back even us Ryug,
defeat the Demon Dukes."{w}{p}"We entrust the fate of the Ryug to you."{w}

"Indeed, my name is Zaalhaut.{w}And what you say is, well, not far off the mark."{w}{p}"Without me, this lot cannot achieve their goal.
Nor can my own wish be fulfilled..."{w}{p}"In any case, you will send this lot
to the Sanctum of Genesis."{w}

"That is none of your concern.{w}Besides, this lot has no path but the Sanctum of Genesis."{w}{p}"Listen well, adventurers."{w}{p}"The Sanctum of Genesis is where Agintaitus and I
once created the Sun Spirit."{w}{p}"Yes, the place where we made Rafa the Sun Spirit."{w}{p}"Back then, Agintaitus and I
were both still far from skilled..."{w}

"With my present power and your help,
we may be able to make Rafa, still incomplete,
into a true Sun Spirit."{w}{p}"If Rafa's power returns, that land will surely be saved too."{w}{p}"Understood, adventurers!?{w}I will be waiting ahead of you at the Sanctum of Genesis. Be sure to come."{w}

A presence of unearthly menace,{w}its massive body twisted and contorted,
was poking its face out of a tiny burrow.{w}{p}Where and how did that body fit inside?{w}Surely it worked by some law
beyond all reckoning.{w}

The fog was thick.{w}It seemed the thing at the heart of the fog{w}was where it came from.{w}{p}All sorts of shadows flickered in the fog.{w}With every passing moment, they changed shape.{w}{p}When the source waved a finger, the shadows vanished.{w}Perhaps even the source itself
was only an illusion.{w}{p}As if it had read that thought,
the source blasted out a great burst of fog.{w}And it grinned.{w}

An old man was sitting quietly.{w}{p}He gave off a presence as though
he had been sitting there
for hundreds of years.{w}{p}The old man's eyes slowly opened{w}and fixed upon you.{w}!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!{w}

{0E}The presence of darkness grew thicker.{0F}
Without enough strength, experience and resolve,
it would be dangerous to go any further. {w}

The Opinion Bits each began to give off light
and started exchanging auras.{w}{p}Before long, the Opinion Bits
all turned toward Zaalhaut at once.{w}
